; Leg DB -- the host SENDS.  The Victor RECEIVES with --rtscts.
;
; THIS IS THE LEG THE SITTING EXISTS FOR.  Same binary as DA, one switch.
; The Victor drops RTS at 256 bytes of ring occupancy and raises it at 64.
; SS16v settled that the host's RTS reaches our CTS; nothing has ever
; measured our RTS reaching the host's, and that is the only thing standing
; between this feature and being on by default.
;
; THE READING IS rxpeak, NOT THE CLOCK, and that is deliberate -- SS16ai's
; rule: when the bench cannot resolve an effect in seconds, find a counter
; that measures the same mechanism.
;
;     rxpeak ~256-600   the host stopped when we asked.  RTS IS WIRED
;                       OUTBOUND.  held/rel > 0 and equal.
;     rxpeak ~2,4xx     we asserted (held>0) and the far end kept sending.
;                       Not wired, or not honoured.  The default stays off
;                       and XON/XOFF is the answer for this cable.
;
; held/rel say WE asserted.  rxpeak says THEY listened.  They are separate
; readings and the leg needs both.
;
; CAVEAT, from SS16ag: rxpeak also moves with retransmissions.  If DA and DB
; do not have the same resend count the comparison is weaker -- but the
; effect here is ~8x and a resend moves it by hundreds, not thousands.

set speed 38400
set receive timeout 20
set retry 30
set parity none
set flow rts/cts
set prefixing cautious
set block 3
log packets s16ajDB.pkt
send rcvdb.dat
statistics
